et","body":"LAR ML (-137) at -137: the algo gave it 57% vs 56% fair (+1.5 pts) — won (+0.7u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 56%). GB ML (+116) at +116: the algo gave it 43% vs 44% fair (-1.5 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 44%). LAR -2.5 (-115) at -115: the algo gave it 53% vs 51% fair (+1.4 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close. GB +2.5 (-104) at -104: the algo gave it 47% vs 49% fair (-1.4 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. OVER 43.5 (-112) at -112: the algo gave it 51% vs 51% fair (+0.6 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. UNDER 43.5 (-107) at -107: the algo gave it 49% vs 49% fair (-0.6 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close.\n\nThe line barely moved between the algo's snapshot and the close.\n\nNo bet: nothing cleared the algo's bar before the game."},{"title":"Where the public and the money were","body":"Splits (Action Network): spread: 50% of bets on Packers, 55% of the money — Rams covered; total: 9% of bets on the over, 5% of the money — it went under; moneyline: 35% of bets on Packers, 49% of the money.\n\nThe sharp side by the algo's read was Packers, who lost and didn't cover."},{"title":"What the algo learns","body":"This game's own lesson: scoring came in at ×0.841 of the raw projection, and the home side beat its projected margin by +5.5 points. It counts toward NFL scoring level, home edge and both teams' attack and defense corrections.\n\nAcross 56 graded NFL games the algo now scales scoring ×0.984 and gives home teams -0.9 points. Team corrections so far: Packers attack ×0.960, defense ×1.040 (4 games); Rams attack ×1.020, defense ×0.960 (4 games)."},{"title":"Bottom line","body":"Right side, total within its normal range, margin within its normal range, no bet."}],"archived":"2026-11-26T04:33:06.842Z"}}}